WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.100
Chris Hardwick: Let's bring out 
the director of Thor Ragnarok,

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.100
an amazing genius that I've been fortunate 
enough to get to know the past few years

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.300
Mr. Taika Watiti!
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.880
Also, a man by the name of

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.880
Chris Hemsworth!

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.880
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.680
Tom Hiddleston!

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.680
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:27.600
Mark Ruffalo!

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.600
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.820
Cate Blanchett!

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:34.820
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.280
A Jeff Goldblum has arrived,
a wild Jeff Goldblum has been spotted.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.100
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:46.120
Also, Tessa Thompson!

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.120
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.500
Karl Urban!

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.060
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.200
And Rachel House!

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:59.200
[Audience cheering and clapping]

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:07.320
Excellent.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.180
Your 'Thor: Ragnarok' cast!

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.180
[Audience cheering]

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.740
Chris Hemsworth: We're here!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.660
Hardwick: Congratulations. Thank you guys 
for being here. Thank you so much for being here.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:21.100
Hemsworth: Thanks for having us.
Hardwick: Uh, Mr. Hemsworth,

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.140
So, Thor does not have his hammer. 
He does not have Asgard. What --

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.300
Hemsworth: Or his hair.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.580
Hardwick: He doesn't have hair, 
that he normally would have.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.160
Hemsworth: No. Getting old, fell out.
[Audience chuckles]

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.500
Hardwick: So this looks like a very different Thor, 
totally, and character wise, with Thor stories.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.560
What's going on? 
What's going on with him right now?

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.440
Hemsworth: Uh, midlife crisis, I think.
[Audience chuckles]

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.820
Um --

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:47.880
Well, I've played this character five times,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.240
uh, this is Marvel's 167th film or something.
[Audience chuckles]

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.700
Um, and --

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.960
Well, me personally, I got a bit bored of myself 
and thought 'we gotta try something different.'

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:03.300
Spoke with Taika, spoke with Kevin, and all of us agreed if we're going to make a third 'Thor,'

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:08.340
we have to really push the envelope and experiment,
and take it to another level, so,

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.400
that was what this film was, you know?

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.920
Cut his hair, break his hammer, 
change his clothes, change the world,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.460
And I think that's what you're going 
to see and be excited about,

00:02:17.460 --> 00:02:22.920
it's something incredibly unique and different for, 
not only the Thor world, but the Marvel universe.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:26.180
[Audience cheering]
Hardwick: And so --

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:29.180
Because he's so used to 
being in charge. I mean like, he's --

00:02:29.180 --> 00:02:32.560
never really seems like 
he has to break much of a sweat.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.080
And this -- but from 
what we've seen so far --

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.580
Hemsworth: No, he gets
his ass kicked in this film.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.980
Mainly by the bloke 
a couple of seats away from me.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.980
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.580
They have a good little rumble, yeah.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.700
Hardwick: And Taika, I was so excited when 
I found out you were doing this movie,

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.020
because 'What We Do In The Shadows' 
is one of the great --

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.020
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.280
You and Jemaine together 
are an incredible combination,

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.480
and to hear that you were going --

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:02.180
What is the transition like from going from 
a film like 'What We Do In The Shadows,'

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.820
which is an intimate movie that 
you worked on for a long time,

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.500
to this, you know, mega-tentpole with 
a character that everyone already knows?

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:14.440
Taika Waititi: Um, yeah, bit of food,
for us now, on set.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.320
And, um --

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.240
You know, I just -- 
just like, um --

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:22.980
You know, Chris was bored of what he was up to,
I was also bored of what he was up to,

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.860
and um --
[Audience laughs]

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.260
And when he reached out,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.600
he rea -- I just saw a friend in need, and, uh --

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.940
[Audience laughs and 'aww's]

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.960
You know. And that's just 
who I am, that's my nature.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.760
[Mark Ruffalo laughs]
Waititi: You know, if you need help,

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:41.460
if you need me to pull you from 
the dark depths, I'm there, for you.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.080
And if that means me having to take on 
a tentpole movie like this,

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:47.280
I'll do it, I'll take one for the team.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.460
[Audience cheers]
So, it's really that.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.600
I was just trying to help my mate out.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.340
Um --

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:59.180
The [indistinct] of how different it was, 
moving from a tiny little film to a giant one,

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:01.380
I feel like --

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.860
There's a lot more pressure, 
obviously, but, um,

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.800
at the end of the day, 
you know, I keep saying this,

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:08.400
whatever's inside that rectangle 
is all that matters.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.820
You know, there might be 
500 more people on the crew, but um,

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.840
you know, as long as 
the actors are good, in their lines,

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:18.400
and, um, saying them, convincingly,
that's all that matters.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.500
Doesn't matter what the budget is.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.500
And --

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.500
Most of these people

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.500
did not learn their lines.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.840
[Audience and panel laugh]

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:32.620
Hardwick: Ok, it just got very serious for a second. 
Let's call people out. Let's make it, uh --

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.360
[Laughter]
Uh, Tom Hiddleston, ah, who --

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:37.360
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.900
Who -- couple years ago, 
you came out here in full costume.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:45.740
There was a full production.
[Audience cheering]

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:50.160
It was one of the most memorable 
and incredible moments of Comic-Con,

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:53.800
and -- you had fun, right? How could you 
not have fun with that? Was that --

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.660
Tom Hiddleston: It was 
a unique experience, and,

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.700
for which I will be 
eternally grateful to Hall H.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.080
[Audience cheering]

00:05:01.080 --> 00:05:04.460
Hardwick: So what what has Loki 
been up to at this point?

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:09.320
Hiddleston: Well, it's been 
four years, and, um --

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:17.140
If you saw 'Thor: The Dark World,' you will know that 
at the end of that film, Loki is on the throne of Asgard,

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:19.060
pretending to be Odin.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.460
So Thor comes home, and, uh, 
things are a little different in Asgard.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.920
Um --

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:31.540
Loki has directed most of his energies
into narcissistic self-glorification.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.880
Um --

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.300
Not so much time on good governance.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.780
Um, but Ragnarok is coming and, uh --

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.080
Loki's allegiances have always 
been slightly unpredictable,

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.460
and he's still the God of Mischief.

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:50.200
And where -- what his part is in all of that,

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:52.280
You'll just have to wait and see.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.240
Hardwick: Alright. I feel like they will,
I feel like they're going to see it.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:58.140
I feel like this crowd is probably gonna 
see this movie. I'm gonna take a guess.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.960
[Audience cheering]
I feel like they're on board with it.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.860
Feel like they're on board with it.

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:05.860
Uh, Mark!
Mark Ruffalo: Uh, yeah.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.260
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.660
I'll go see it. I'm gonna see it. 
I'll see it.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:12.520
Hardwick: You're gonna see it? 
Ruffalo: I'll -- I'm gonna see it.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:16.060
Hardwick: Can you pick me up? Can you take me -- 
can you out to see the movie? I want to see the movie.

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.580
What -- can we talk about 
the evolution of the Hulk a little bit?

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.820
Ruffalo: What is it?
Hardwick: The evolution of the Hulk.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.520
The Hulk is a movie that you -- 
you're a character in the --

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.520
Ruffalo: Oh!

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:30.340
Well, it's a little different Hulk 
than we've seen. He, um --

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:33.280
Hulk refuses to turn back into Banner.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.900
And he's actually enjoying 
his time on Sakaar,

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:44.360
because he is a Gladiator Champion 
of the world of Sakaar.

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:46.960
Which means he kicks a lot of "A".

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.300
[Audience chuckles]

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:53.520
Because it says right here, 'please be aware that many members of your audience may be under the age of 18.'

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.200
Hardwick: It is very nice of you to honor that.

00:06:56.200 --> 00:06:59.220
Literally nobody else has been honoring that.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:01.720
Ruffalo: He kicks a lot of "A". 
Hardwick: Nice.

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:05.500
And and he's enjoying his life for once,

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.220
and he'll be damned 
if he's going to go back to Banner.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.680
Hardwick: Again with the harsh language. 
I don't know why you had to take it so fluffy [?] there.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.760
[Audience laughs]

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.680
Ruffalo: Is 'damn' a swear word? 
Hardwick: I don't know, probably not.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.060
I just think, kids, you can't 
offend them at all anymore,

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.520
because of the internet, it doesn't even 
matter anymore, everyone knows everything.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.660
[Audience chuckles]
Ahh --

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:26.020
So is he sort of -- he is kind of a perma-Hulk at this point?

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.620
Ruffalo: He's a little perma-Hulked.
Hardwick: Yeah.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:30.400
Ruffalo: Um -- and,

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:32.380
He's starting to be able --

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:38.000
because he's been the Hulk for two years now, 
he has a vocabulary of a two-year-old.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.240
[Audience chuckles]

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.100
So we have a speaking Hulk.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.220
Can I say that?
Waititi: Well, too late.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:45.660
Ruffalo: Alright, sorry.
[Audience laughs]

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:50.880
We may or may not 
have a speaking Hulk, in 'Thor 3,'

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:53.560
where everyone may or may not die.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.200
[Audience and panel laughter]

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.460
Hardwick: Fair enough. That wraps it up.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:00.260
Ah, Cate. How did you come 
into the Marvel Universe?

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.260
And what was your --
[Audience cheering]

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:05.640
What -- what -- 
what threw you in --

00:08:05.640 --> 00:08:09.600
I mean seriously, yeah, seriously. 
Seriously, seriously.

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:12.460
Cate Blanchett: A sort of happy accident.

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:15.880
I sort of live in the same continent 
as Taika, and the flight was cheap,

00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:17.820
so he came over and --
[Hardwick laughs]

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.180
Waititi: I just saw a friend in need.
[Audience laughter]

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.560
You know? Someone just 
reaching out for [indistinct].

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.340
A whisper in the dark, 
just, yeah, needing help.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.480
Blanchett: Yeah, no, I'm grateful.
No, I mean -- look, it's -- it's, um --

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:38.860
it's a universe that I've sort of been
happily dragged into, because of my kids.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:44.240
And yeah, so yeah, 
and to work with Taika, and these guys,

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.820
and gal-s [emphasizes the plural],
was, yeah, pretty exciting.

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:50.260
Hardwick: Pretty amazing.
And then, uh, Jeff Goldblum, who --

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.260
[Audience cheering and clapping]
The Grandmaster.

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:57.000
If I'm not mistaken, you're the -- yes.

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.000
Jeff Goldblum: No, you were gonna say.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Hardwick: You're the Collector's brother, 
is that not, uh, accurate?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.000
Goldblum: He looks like what?
Hardwick: The Coll -- you're --

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.840
[Audience chuckles]
Blanchett: It's hard to hear.

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.240
Hardwick: [increases volume]
Oh, it is hard to hear?

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.100
[shouting] 
You are the Collector's brother!

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:11.020
Goldblum: Yes, I'm the Collector's brother.

00:09:11.020 --> 00:09:15.200
Benicio Del Toro. Yes, yes.
[Audience cheering]

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.020
We're very old, we were -- we were elders -- 
we're elders of the universe.

00:09:20.020 --> 00:09:22.260
We came about shortly after the Big Bang.

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.560
Ruffalo: So did the rest of us.
[Hardwick and audience laugh]

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:31.260
Hardwick: Aww, come on.

00:09:31.260 --> 00:09:34.700
It's really funny, you make that joke, but 
you say "A" instead of ass. That's really funny.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.310
[Audience chuckles]

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:40.920
Goldblum: My character, yeah, we're all the -- 
we're the oldest living creatures in the universe.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:44.780
Yeah, oldest living race, 
they call us in the thing.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:47.240
We were here 
shortly after the Big Bang.

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:51.520
Grandmaster, and, um, 
and my brother Collector. That's right.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:54.580
Hardwick: Excellent.
Goldblum: And now I run -- [chuckles]

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:59.020
And now I rule on this planet Sakaar, 
and put together games, mostly.

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:01.160
I'm a games -- I love games.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:02.940
[Audience chuckles]

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:06.440
And fighting, fighting games, 
and I put together,

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:10.580
I don't want to give anything away,
but the great, great match between

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.800
Hulk and the new Thor.

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.100
[Audience clapping and cheering]
I put that together.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:19.780
For your entertainment and pleasure.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.040
Hardwick: Can you hear me down there, Tessa? 
Can you hear me here?

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.220
Tessa Thompson: Yeah, I can hear you.
Hardwick: Oh ok, great. Ah, welcome, welcome.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:28.620
[Audience clapping and cheering]
Thompson: Thanks very much.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:33.320
Hardwick: So what can you say about Valkyries, or 
anything you can say about Valkyrie, for people?

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.700
Thompson: Uh, you know,
I was just another friend in need.

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:39.340
[Hardwick laughs]

00:10:39.340 --> 00:10:42.520
Waititi: You're welcome.
[Audience chuckles]

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:47.140
Thompson: No, I'm thankful.
Uh, she's an elite warrior of Asgard,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.000
who's hanging out on Sakaar
for reasons that I can't really elaborate on.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.640
And she has a relationship 
with the Grandmaster.

00:10:54.640 --> 00:10:56.540
It's not romantic.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:59.440
I mean, maybe it 
used to be. Who knows?

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:01.180
Um -- 
[Audience laughs]

00:11:01.180 --> 00:11:03.180
He's a friend from work.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:04.680
[Audience laughs]

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:07.380
And, uh --

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:10.700
I just -- she just picks up 
little pieces around town

00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:15.100
and maybe an interesting 
one of them happens to be a big...

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:19.020
God-like thing. Um -- yeah, right?

00:11:19.020 --> 00:11:23.140
And so she brings him 
to the Grandmaster, and then,

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.220
it takes us off on our story.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:27.880
Hardwick: Excellent.
Karl Urban, who's, uh, Skurge.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.880
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:33.660
Karl Urban: Comic-Con, how are you?
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:38.860
Are you out of your Vulcan mind?
[Audience clapping and cheering]

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:41.560
Hardwick: Ah, yeah.
Urban: [indistinct] we?

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.520
Hardwick: Cross the streams, man. 
I love it. Cross the streams.

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.520
[Audience laughs]

00:11:48.260 --> 00:11:51.700
They -- when did you guys shoot this movie? 
Because they said you shaved your head,

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:56.140
and you already have -- like, you're that masculine, 
that your hair immediately just, whoof.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:01.540
Urban: Yeah, uh, I was in the same boat 
with everybody else, actually,

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:07.300
I was actually on vacation, and I received a call from 
Taika, who was in Australia, deep behind enemy lines.

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.980
[Hardwick and audience laugh]

00:12:08.980 --> 00:12:11.660
Saying, 'mate, uh, I need help.'

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:15.720
And so literally, that is why I joined this cast.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:19.580
Uh, so it's --
Waititi: Karl's from New Zealand, like me,

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:23.280
and, you know, 
surrounded by so many Australians,

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.820
it's just the accent, it's just --
Urban: Yeah. It's a little bit --

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.640
Waititi: -- drilled, I think, drilled into 
the side of the head, all day long.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:30.600
[Audience laughs]

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.860
Like a glass bottle, full of nails, 
just shake them in your ears, like all day.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:38.180
Urban: You know, 
I almost didn't make it to set,

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:42.760
because when I came into Australia, the customs 
officer asked me if I had a criminal record,

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.940
and I said, 'Oh mate, I didn't know 
I still needed one to get in!'

00:12:45.940 --> 00:12:47.940
[Hardwick and audience laugh]

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:57.460
Chris Hemsworth, 
your great-granddaddy stole an apple,

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.920
[Audience chuckles]

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.920
got caught, and was 
sent on a boat, right?

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.820
Hemsworth: Thank God, 
thank God for that, too.

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:06.640
Hardwick: Breaking news! Australia declares war 
on New Zealand, tomorrow at 11.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.900
Hemsworth: Yeah, we're just kind of bridging the gap 
between New Zealand and Australia, for the moment.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:14.760
As you can see, we're sitting a lot closer 
to each other, than shooting at --

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:18.020
Waititi: Bringing two cultures together, 
the warring tribes of Australia and New Zealand.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:20.020
Hemsworth: It's all over. In the past.
Waititi: Long [?] peace.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.020
[Audience laughs]

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.620
Hardwick: Make! A! Baby! 
Make! A! Baby!

00:13:27.620 --> 00:13:29.240
[Audience chuckles]

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.780
Hemsworth: We will.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:33.240
We made a movie, instead.

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:36.040
Hardwick: And then Rachel House,
who has a -- a history of --

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.040
[Audience and panel clapping and cheering]

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.240
-- working with Taika, and --
Rachel House: None of you know who I am.

00:13:40.240 --> 00:13:41.660
Hardwick: -- people who don't know, 
can you talk about some of your --

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:43.200
House: It's very nice 
that you're cheering. Hello.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.360
Hardwick: Hello.
House: Hello!

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.240
Hardwick: Can you talk about 
your history a little bit, working with Taika?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:49.800
House: So I've been in 4 out of 5 
of his films that he's made, yeah.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:53.340
So he just pulled me along 
for the accent, and for the ride.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:57.740
Waititi: Yeah, Rachel's like my good-luck charm, 
I try and put her in everything I do.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:02.160
'Cause, uh, she's... 
you just gotta see her, she's awesome.

